1
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:47,860
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:50,870
[Episode 11]

3
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,840
Chief Chen, let me introduce myself.

4
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,590
I'm Ma Feiyan

5
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:01,190
from Ma Construction Group.

6
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,350
Starting today,

7
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:04,480
I'll be fully in charge of
the factory construction

8
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:07,080
and village relocation plan
of Shapu Village.

9
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,310
Ms. Ma?

10
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:12,800
What about Mr. Huang from before?

11
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,680
It's Ma Construction Group.

12
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,960
How much pull do you think

13
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,400
this Huang has?

14
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:22,240
This is

15
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:24,280
my newly drafted
relocation compensation plan.

16
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,560
The compensation
was 2,400 per square meter,

17
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,090
and I've raised it to 3,000.

18
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,560
And I've also offered the villagers

19
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,000
even better conditions.

20
00:02:32,710 --> 00:02:34,040
You can take a good look.

21
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,960
Is our village really worth that much?

22
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:41,550
Are you sure you won't lose money?

23
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:44,400
You don't need to worry about that.

24
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,360
I heard the person making the movie
in your village

25
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,750
is an extra from Shudian

26
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:50,310
and a few kids, right?

27
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:53,470
This kind of playing house

28
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,750
is never going to work.

29
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:56,280
You see, besides me,

30
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,310
do you have a better choice?

31
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:04,010
Let me... think about it.

32
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,590
Chief Chen,

33
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,620
I'm really here in good faith.

34
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:14,270
Anyone who comes to sign the contract
before noon tomorrow

35
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:15,670
will be paid on the spot.

36
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:22,030
Fellow villagers!

37
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,090
Fellow villagers!

38
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:24,750
I have good news to announce!

39
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:27,560
Those who agree to the relocation,

40
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,140
please come to
the village committee office

41
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,700
and sign the consent form
by noon tomorrow.

42
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,280
You'll get paid on the spot!

43
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,430
They really will pay us on the spot?

44
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:39,510
Will they?

45
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,100
Attention, everyone!

46
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:49,400
Villagers who haven't signed yet,

47
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,030
please hurry to the village committee
to do it!

48
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:53,560
Ms. Ma will extend

49
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,160
the signing time by one hour!

50
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,090
You will be paid on the spot!

51
00:03:59,150 --> 00:03:59,610
Jiaoqi.

52
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:02,040
Drink it while it's hot.

53
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:04,010
My pour-over... instant coffee.

54
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:04,960
Look at the time.

55
00:04:05,430 --> 00:04:06,870
How are you still in the mood for coffee?

56
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:07,400
Jiaoqi.

57
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,280
I think Mr. Huang's sister-in-law

58
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,990
is not someone to be trifled with.

59
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:15,250
Looks like Mr. Huang is doomed this time.

60
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:18,269
What are you talking about?

61
00:04:18,269 --> 00:04:19,560
Mr. Huang never fails.

62
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,600
Well...

63
00:04:21,829 --> 00:04:23,950
Ma Feiyan is quite something.

64
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:26,120
Why don't we join her?

65
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:27,120
I...

66
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,070
Do you have a conscience saying that?

67
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:30,160
If it weren't for Mr. Huang,

68
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:30,830
your whole family—

69
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,070
your aunts and uncles—

70
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:33,340
would all be starving!

71
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,750
No, I was just thinking...

72
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:37,600
I heard Ma Feiyan is single.

73
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:38,720
I thought I'd give it a shot

74
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,650
and win her over.

75
00:04:39,909 --> 00:04:40,909
I'll do it myself.

76
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,390
I'd be a better option than you.

77
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:47,480
Of course I can't do it.

78
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,540
I have your sister.

79
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,070
Jiaoqi,

80
00:04:51,870 --> 00:04:53,070
worst comes to worst,

81
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:54,480
let's join Zhen.

82
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:57,750
I...

83
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,560
You're just a traitor.

84
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:02,720
Come on. You won't allow us

85
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,870
to join any side.

86
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:05,950
Have you learned any other tricks
from Romance of the Three Kingdoms?

87
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:07,310
I'm not reading it anymore.

88
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,750
It's all about schemes and plots.
It's useless.

89
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,280
I should read Water Margin.

90
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,310
You mean the part where

91
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,950
Pan Jinlian poisons Wu Dalang?

92
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,280
That is indeed impressive.

93
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:18,950
But no.

94
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:20,640
Come here.

95
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:45,570
Why are you here alone?

96
00:05:46,270 --> 00:05:47,150
I'm leaving.

97
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:51,080
So I'm taking one last look
at our village.

98
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,800
Such a nice village.

99
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,610
It's a pity it's being demolished.

100
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:02,330
How is it going now?

101
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,860
Many people have already signed.

102
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:07,040
Will you?

103
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:10,030
It doesn't matter whether I sign or not.

104
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,420
It won't change anything anyway.

105
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,750
I'm sorry.

106
00:06:16,430 --> 00:06:17,830
I wasn't able to help you.

107
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:19,640
You've tried your best.

108
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:22,870
You're the one who tried your best.

109
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:24,920
I think it's my fault.

110
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,230
Whenever I make a movie,
it never ends well.

111
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:29,430
Maybe this is fate.

112
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,260
I've dragged you down.

113
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:33,650
I think you did a great job.

114
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,409
I really like it.

115
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:39,800
Really?

116
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:44,040
Thank you.

117
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,480
I think the ones you made before

118
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,810
must be pretty good too.

119
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:50,390
You should share them with everyone.

120
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,000
Do you want to watch them?

121
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,140
There will be a chance.

122
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:03,130
There will be a chance.

123
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:05,630
When are you leaving?

124
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:07,430
Tomorrow.

125
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:12,350
Then I have to give you
a proper farewell tonight.

126
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:13,910
Thank you.

127
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:20,250
After the village is demolished,

128
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:21,930
what are your plans?

129
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:23,510
Go home.

130
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,200
Don't you live here?

131
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,260
Then where do you live?

132
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,310
In the sea.

133
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,270
Actually, I'm a mermaid.

134
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,000
I just came ashore a few years ago.

135
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,600
Look, these aren't legs.

136
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,120
You really believe that?

137
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,080
You have a great mindset.

138
00:07:43,310 --> 00:07:44,640
I should learn from you.

139
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:46,720
What else can I do?

140
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,680
Can I visit your home?

141
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:49,270
Sure.

142
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:51,480
I'll treat you to my neighbors.

143
00:07:51,770 --> 00:07:53,220
How do I find you in the sea?

144
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,350
Just go into the sea.

145
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:56,270
When you hear "woo-hoo-hoo-hoo,

146
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:57,270
woo-hoo-hoo-hoo,"

147
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:58,190
that'll be me.

148
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:00,430
But I can't swim.

149
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,060
Then I'll give you a secret signal to use.

150
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:03,750
I'll come ashore to pick you up.

151
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:04,480
What signal?

152
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,120
Work harder! Keep on!

153
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:10,750
Come on!

154
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:15,920
Come on!

155
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:21,240
-Work harder! Keep on!
-Work harder! Keep on!

156
00:08:34,909 --> 00:08:35,630
Are you done picking?

157
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:36,690
How much for these?

158
00:08:36,909 --> 00:08:37,909
And a lollipop.

159
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:39,770
Why did you take so many?

160
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:41,080
To eat on the way.

161
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,530
You're leaving?

162
00:08:47,390 --> 00:08:48,250
I'm going back.

163
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,090
I asked you how much.

164
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,720
It's on the house.

165
00:08:56,910 --> 00:08:58,170
Then can you not leave?

166
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,150
Am I that cheap?

167
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:05,600
What?

168
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:07,360
Just stay.

169
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,030
Do I have any reason to stay?

170
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:11,870
I...

171
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:18,480
I... Our village is pretty good.

172
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:18,960
Look.

173
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:21,630
Good views...

174
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,050
and good people.

175
00:09:26,910 --> 00:09:28,440
Everyone else is pretty good.

176
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,630
But you...

177
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:32,270
Haven't I turned over a new leaf?

178
00:09:32,270 --> 00:09:33,530
That's all in the past.

179
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,390
Really.

180
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:36,430
Really. Look.

181
00:09:36,790 --> 00:09:37,590
The mountain.

182
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:40,010
The water, the fishing boats,

183
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,940
and this little store.

184
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:46,510
No seaweed. I'm giving you a bad review.

185
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,790
What?

186
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:52,590
Can I ask you to film things for me
in the future?

187
00:09:52,590 --> 00:09:53,720
You can't afford me.

188
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,050
What do you want to film?

189
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:57,720
Well...

190
00:10:00,270 --> 00:10:01,320
My WeChat...

191
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,240
My Moments...

192
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,200
Silly.

193
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,150
What?

194
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,510
Can I call you?

195
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,330
Don't call too early in the morning.

196
00:10:12,330 --> 00:10:13,130
I can't get up.

197
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,840
Shave that toothbrush moustache
when you have time.

198
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,700
It looks dirty.

199
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:25,910
And also,

200
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:28,960
can you not use a straw
when you drink cola next time?

201
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:29,890
It's very girly.

202
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:42,630
Can't I be the reason you stay?

203
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,660
Why couldn't I just say it?

204
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:52,630
Sea!

205
00:10:52,810 --> 00:10:53,600
Stop yelling!

206
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,120
I'm...

207
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,200
It's bedtime!

208
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:56,750
Don't you know?

209
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:57,670
Come on!

210
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:07,200
♪ Outside the long corridor,
along the ancient road ♪

211
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:12,270
♪ Green grass extending to the sky ♪

212
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:19,750
♪ If only we had some wine to celebrate ♪

213
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:25,320
♪ Then it wouldn't be so cold tonight ♪

214
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:32,690
Thank you, Jiahao.

215
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,000
We...

216
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,650
Jiahao, you've sung this already.

217
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,320
But today,

218
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,600
I already can't...

219
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,080
Jiahao.

220
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,600
-Leave you!
-Jiahao.

221
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:50,440
It's the same song.

222
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,120
It's the same song.

223
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,780
You've sung it several times.

224
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:54,750
Thank you. Thank you.

225
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,510
Mr. Zhou!

226
00:11:58,110 --> 00:12:00,240
It's fine. It's okay.

227
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:03,610
It's not like
we'll never see each other again.

228
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:05,990
What's going on here?

229
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,490
He's singing for me.

230
00:12:08,510 --> 00:12:09,570
To... to see me off.

231
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,600
I thought it was a karaoke night.

232
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:12,720
I could hear you from far away,

233
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:13,840
singing so loudly.

234
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,840
Ms. Lin!

235
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,590
Everything will be alright.

236
00:12:18,590 --> 00:12:19,990
Everything will be fine.

237
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,120
Well... wait for me here.

238
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,910
I have a gift for you.

239
00:12:25,910 --> 00:12:26,790
No, no. You don't have to.

240
00:12:26,790 --> 00:12:28,720
-Wait for me. Don't go.
-Jiahao...

241
00:12:46,910 --> 00:12:47,910
Are you okay?

242
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:50,720
I'm fine.

243
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:52,850
And you?

244
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:54,870
I'm fine too.

245
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,660
Oh, right, Jiahao.

246
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,600
I've washed all the clothes
I borrowed from you

247
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,360
and hung them up.

248
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,100
Thank you for letting me borrow them.

249
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:11,100
You can keep them.

250
00:13:11,150 --> 00:13:12,120
No, really, no need.

251
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:13,270
I just needed them for the time being.

252
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:15,200
We're close enough to share pants!

253
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:15,670
No need.

254
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,510
How about this? You take the green ones.

255
00:13:17,510 --> 00:13:19,310
They're too short for me anyway.

256
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,630
-Alright.
-I'll take them.

257
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:21,200
Take them.

258
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,670
I'll wear them on the road tomorrow.

259
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:23,600
Thanks, Jiahao.

260
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,750
This... is a photo of me and my sister.

261
00:13:32,710 --> 00:13:33,470
I hope

262
00:13:34,510 --> 00:13:36,040
you'll always remember us.

263
00:13:39,870 --> 00:13:41,000
Just take it.

264
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:44,190
That's very thoughtful.

265
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,600
And Stephen Chow?

266
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:50,720
This is my dad.

267
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,150
They look so alike?

268
00:13:53,150 --> 00:13:53,630
Do they?

269
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,240
I...

270
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,960
Taking your dad's photo would be...

271
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:57,440
Well...

272
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,360
I'll take my dad's photo out
before giving it to you.

273
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,420
They look so alike.

274
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:03,040
It's not appropriate for me to take it.

275
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:05,440
This is... Well...

276
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,040
Open it and see for yourself.

277
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,540
I sometimes see you staring at it

278
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:17,670
and spacing out.

279
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:20,640
I think you must really like him.

280
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:24,690
I hope that no matter
what happens in the future,

281
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:26,360
or what setbacks you face,

282
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,220
you'll remember these two lines.

283
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,080
Thank you.

284
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:33,420
You too.

285
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:35,810
I'll take it.

286
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:37,870
Work harder! Keep on!

287
